hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1350","Ahmad ibn Abduh informed us, Abd al-Warith ibn Sa`id informed us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir ibn Abdullah, that The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, led his companions with the prayer of fear, and they all knelt down, then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prostrated, and the row of He and the others would stand until when he got up, they would prostrate themselves twice, then the front row would be delayed until they would stand up with those. These people moved around until they took the place of the front row, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, knelt with them all, then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prostrated. And the row after him, when they raised their heads, they prostrated twice. All of them kneeled with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and prostrated. They prostrated themselves twice, and the enemy was near the Qiblah.”"
